Z||000000||htiek||10-26-2001||09:56 AM||||Two nights ago I was driving back to my dorm around 230 in the morning.  As i drive i always try to figure out what kind of car is either following or coming at me by there headlights, well i was seeing the usual cars, hondas, bmw's, mustangs and other such cars.  Then coming at me was a set of headlights that were really low to the ground, and i figured that someone had really slammed there car to the floor, but no it wasnt any car that i had seen around before.  When it passed i realized it was a beautiful bright yellow Ferrari.  <P>As soon as i noticed what it was i pulled into a convenience store parking lot and having nothing to do whipped back onto the road and followed it for a couple of miles, then i guess he noticed me following him so he sped up, Ok he blew me away, even though we werent racing i had no chance in hell in keeping up with him as he wanted to show me nothing but the faint flow of his tailights from as far down the road as possible.  <P>All i can say is that it was an interesting 10 minutes, interesting but fun.||||reg||6
Z||000001||Don_Chi_Chi||10-26-2001||10:09 AM||||What kind of Ferarri was it?  Pretty much any one made could smoke a stock fiero.<P>------------------<BR>Previously known as Saleenfiero||||reg||1
Z||000002||htiek||10-26-2001||10:23 AM||||Sorry, it was a ferrari 348 as far as i could tell, bright yellow, and your right any ferrari would of blown my car away, i was just hoping that maybe he would notice me and pull over so that i could get a closer look.  <P>Thats all!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Screwie||10-26-2001||02:53 PM||||Well, I lived in London (UK) for a while. You see ferrari's there every day (really!) Cool though, one was parked and had a glass panel so you could see the engine!! Needless to say, I was looking at it for a loooong while. But what was really cool, there was a purple Lamborghini driving around my neighbourhood! The sound of that thing roaring, whaaa, I love it. <BR>Btw: if you ever go to London and think your Porsche or Lotus is cool, think twice, there just as normal there as a Ford in the US. So if you do go, I'd advice you to take your Fiero, that's a sight they don't get to see very often over there!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
